      "utf8": "or click that link down\nin the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015040,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to thank Nord VPN\nfor sponsoring this part of the video,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017760,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and now\nback to Bell's theorem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020160,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The EPR paper certainly got a lot\nof attention."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023680,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Without asking Einstein,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024880,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Podolsky leaked\nthe paper to the press"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026720,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the story ended up\nin the New York Times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028800,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Prodigious harvest of the day's."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030960,
    "dDurationMs": 1598,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "intelligence is reached.\n- Extra, extra"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032558,
    "dDurationMs": 2002,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- read all about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034560,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein was the most famous\nscientist in the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037040,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he was going after the strange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038480,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but successful theory\nof quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So of course the press loved it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1042880,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what did scientists\nthink of the argument itself?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046600,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the reaction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the physics community\nwas at first mixed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052160,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, there were some\npeople, sort of old allies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1054560,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Einstein's who were very happy with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Schrodinger being sort of\nat the top of that list."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060880,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in fact, in an\nattempt to clear up some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063520,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the misunderstandings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064480,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that people were having\nabout the EPR paper,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066880,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Schrodinger publishes the\nthought experiment known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as Schrodinger's cat,\nsort of back up Einstein"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071920,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and show the kind of problem that he"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075280,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Einstein had with quantum physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or meanwhile, it's like, oh my God, what?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080960,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What the hell is this?\nHe must be wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083680,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How do we show that he's wrong?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1085360,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then Bohr ultimately, you\nknow, in his sort of painful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and complicated style ends\nup coming up with a response"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092560,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the EPR paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094160,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This response is sort of famously obscure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096640,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and difficult to understand and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098400,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I have, I have read it in detail"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I will tell you\nBohr's reply is either"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104560,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nonsensical or makes\nsome actual mistakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1107280,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There is a very well turned sentence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110640,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which I believe Bohr took a great deal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112640,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of trouble in formulating,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and his meaning is just\nabsolutely obscure to me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1118240,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Bohr said in his reply to\nEPR, in his multiple replies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122560,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to EPR,\nthat there is no question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124720,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of anything non-local going on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1127200,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the ultimate reaction\nof the physics community,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130400,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least in the immediate years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131760,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and decades following\nthe publication of EPR"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Bohr's reply in 1935, was to think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138080,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Bohr had settled it with his reply,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though people didn't really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1143120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understand what Bohr had said."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Two decades later, Einstein\ndied still questioning quantum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148720,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mechanics, but the majority"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150240,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the physics community had\nmoved on without him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bohr however,\nnever forgot about the EPR paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156880,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1962,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1158240,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "7 years after Einstein's death,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160320,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bohr gave an interview about Einstein"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1162640,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he lamented that Einstein\nwasted decades on fruitless"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1165840,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thought experiments\nbecause he simply could not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167920,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accept quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169680,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "'It was terrible that Einstein\nfell in that trap to work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with Podolsky' Bohr said,\nRosen is worse from my point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175840,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of view, Rosen, even today believes the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "EPR thought experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179280,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Podolsky has given it up,\nas far as I know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181680,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole idea\nis absolutely nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1183600,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When one really gets\ninto it, you may think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1186560,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I say it too\nstrongly, but it is true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189200,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's absolutely no problem in it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next day, Bohr took a nap\nafter lunch and never woke up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196800,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so after many decades,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Einstein-Bohr debate was over."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bohr's authority was part"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1202720,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the reason the EPR paper\ndidn't get the attention it deserved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206160,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there was another reason"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1207520,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicists ignored it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208720,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the EPR experiment, both theories,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210560,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Copenhagen Quantum Mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211920,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Einstein's local hidden\nvariable alternative make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215040,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly the same prediction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216800,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You get the same results either way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1218880,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "debating two different interpretations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1220640,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the same experimental\nresult seemed like armchair"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "philosophy, not real physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1225440,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Copenhagen interpretation\nmakes good predictions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1227920,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so why not just teach that and move on?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just seems like, you know, shut up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232800,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and calculate, I think is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234560,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "message that kind of gets pushed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- General attitude was,\nthis is done, who cares?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "None of this matters. It's all settled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1243200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein and Bohr had a big\ndebate about it and Bohr won."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246960,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you think you're\nsmarter than Niels Bohr?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1249040,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you think you're smarter\nthan Albert Einstein?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250760,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It seemed like it would be impossible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253120,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to resolve this debate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1254480,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until another physicist\nturned his attention to it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1258320,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "John Bell was an\nundergraduate student shortly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260480,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after World War II in\nthis new era of physics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263600,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so of course,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264640,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was taught the\nCopenhagen Interpretation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1266400,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- John Bell's doubts\nabout quantum mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269040,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by his own recollection, showed up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1272480,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basically the minute he learned it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274160,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In his first quantum mechanics\nclass, he was, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "getting pretty upset with the instructors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and saying, you're being too vague."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What the heck do you\nmean about measurement?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285760,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Bell was never fully satisfied"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the answers he got\nabout the foundations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289520,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1290720,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when he was doing his\nPhD, he was encouraged"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1293040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to study something a little\nbit more respectable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1295680,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so he studied nuclear physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1297200,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and went on to have a very\naccomplished career at Cern."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1300320,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But after eight years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301520,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of working in particle physics,\nin 1963,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1303920,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he took an academic sabbatical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305760,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and finally he had time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1306960,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to focus on his doubts\nabout quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1310000,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He said, I always knew\nthat it was waiting for me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314800,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He began by re-examining the old debates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316960,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the papers that most\nphysicists had long since dismissed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1319600,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as philosophical distractions,\nincluding the EPR paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1323600,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After this research, he said,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1324800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "'I felt that Einstein's intellectual\nsuperiority over Bohr in this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328400,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instance was enormous;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329920,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've vast gulf between\nthe man who saw clearly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1332160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what was needed and the obscurantist.'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He realized Einstein's logic was sound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337280,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the two conclusions is true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1339360,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The question was, could\nyou prove which one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1341840,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "using an experiment?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1343680,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An experiment of this sort seemed much\nmore feasible by Bell's time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1347440,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The EPR paper was the first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to consider the idea of entanglement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1351200,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These days, entanglement is a core feature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1353200,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1354560,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Einstein had been first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355920,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to even point out entanglement existed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358640,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why the EPR paper was\nset up as a thought experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1361760,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because no one had made\nsuch an exotic state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of matter in 1935."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1366080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in the intervening decades\nbetween Einstein's work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1368560,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Bell's between 1935"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1370320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 1964, entanglement\nhad become a serious topic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1373760,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of study.\nBy Bell's time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1375520,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there were reliable ways\nto make it in the lab."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1377840,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, Madam Wu had famously\nreproduced the EPR thought"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experiment as a real experiment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383200,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but simply doing the EPR\nexperiment in real life isn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1386160,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enough to tell you which\nexplanation is correct since"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1389120,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both predict the same thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Bell wondered if\nthere was another version"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392960,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the experiment where the non-local"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1394800,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and local theories would have\nto give a different result."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397560,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you're asking that question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1399600,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you're playing with the\nEPR setup, then it's like, oh,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1403040,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's literally not just\nfiguratively a twist. Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407400,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Here's a simplified\nversion of bell's experiment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1411040,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make your entangled\nelectron and positron again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413840,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now, instead of just measuring them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a Stern–Gerlach machine like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1417440,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the experimenters get a choice about how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1419920,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to orient their machine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1421360,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The three different choices\nare zero degrees, 120 degrees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1424960,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 240 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426960,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the twist on the EPR experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1429680,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The experimenters get\nto choose independently,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432080,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the electron might be measured\nat zero degrees while the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1434720,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positron is measured at 240 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1438000,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If both experimenters happen\nto choose the same axis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440560,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then we know what happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1442000,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have to get the\nopposite result as each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1444400,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to conserve spin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1446080,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The interesting case is when\nthe experimenters happen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to choose different\naxes, the number we want"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1451920,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to predict here is the\ndisagreement rate, the probability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1454560,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the electron's result is\ndifferent from the positron's."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1457720,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At first, let's see what quantum mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460400,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "predicts for this number."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1463600,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's say the electron is\nmeasured with the zero degree axis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1466160,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and comes out as plus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1468000,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that its spin has\ncollapsed to positive Z,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1470400,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the positron spin needs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471680,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to instantly collapse to be negative Z."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1474000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the non-local\npart of quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1476880,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but what happens when\nthis positron is measured"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1478800,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by a machine tilted at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1482240,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the positron spin is already\nalmost facing the plus end"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1485440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the machine, so it's much\nmore likely to go to plus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489120,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, there's a 75%\nchance it goes to plus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491680,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and only a 25% chance it goes to minus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1494400,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the disagreement rate is 25%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497360,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can show that for\nany two different axes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1499600,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the experimenters select,\nthe geometry is analogous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they all have this same\ndisagreement rate of 25%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1507600,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anytime the experimenters\nchoose different axes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1510080,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they will get the same\noutcomes 75% of the time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512720,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and different outcomes 25% of the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1515680,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now, let's consider\nthe local hidden variable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518480,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alternative theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The particles here are\non a mission, their aim"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523200,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make you believe that\nthey're acting according"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1525440,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to quantum mechanics when\nreally they're acting locally."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1529520,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we are anthropomorphizing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1531200,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I think it is really useful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1532720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to just imagine them this way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1534400,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're trying to figure out if\nit's always possible for them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to use a hidden variable theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539200,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get the same experimental outcomes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1541680,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as Copenhagen quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1544000,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or if in this new situation\nour scheming particles won't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1547920,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be able to fool us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of it like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each of the particles\nis gonna be asked one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554560,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of three possible questions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1556880,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they need to decide on\ntheir answer while they're still"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "together so that they can\ncoordinate on their strategy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1563920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When they're done figuring out a plan for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1566080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how they would answer any\nof the three questions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1569040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they pack away those hidden\nvariables into three sealed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1572960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "envelopes for each particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575280,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The question is, what strategies\nshould our sneaky particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1578800,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take to make people believe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1580560,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they're following quantum mechanics?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Remember, quantum mechanics\npredicted a disagreement rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1586400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 25%, and so our particles\nwant to match that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1591600,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whenever they happen to be\nasked different questions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1594560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their answer needs to disagree\nabout 25% of the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1599120,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what's the best strategy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1601440,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, there's actually only two things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1603120,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they really can do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1604960,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first strategy is this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1606800,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The electron answers the\nsame way for each of its axes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1610080,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the positron answers\nin the opposite way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1612960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's say the electron answers with minus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1617680,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the positron with plus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1622720,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is a terrible idea"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1624720,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because whatever two different\naxes the experimenters happen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1628400,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to choose, the disagreement\nrate is a hundred percent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1632800,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is very different from 25%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1635040,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so that strategy doesn't work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637200,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there's only one other strategy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1638880,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the particles could use."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1640880,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of the electron\ndoing exactly the same thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1643600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for all three axes, it does\nthe same thing for any two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647520,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of its axes and then something\ndifferent for the last one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1651120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's just say for\nexample, that it does this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655280,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then the positron does the opposite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1657680,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is just one example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it turns out for all\npossible strategies like this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1661680,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the disagreement rate\nis gonna be the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1665040,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's imagine first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1666240,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the experimenter who's\nmeasuring the electron happens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1669520,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to measure it in the 120 degree axis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1672720,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it gets the answer\nminus they make this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1675680,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "choice a third of the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1677760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now to calculate the\ndisagreement rate, we need to see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1680960,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what happens when the\nexperimenter who's measuring the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1683840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positron happens to measure a\ndifferent axis from this one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1688000,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So one of these two,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1689920,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but in either one of these cases,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691440,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the positron is also a minus,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1693360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so the two answers\nagree with each other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1696400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so the answers have no disagreement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1699120,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so we can multiply this by zero,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1704560,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but two thirds of the time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1705680,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the experimenter who's measuring\nthe electron will happen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1708480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to measure it in one\nof the other two axes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711120,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's say this one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1717040,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the experimenter measuring\nthe positron will measure in one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1719840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of these two axes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1721280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you can see\nthat they only pick an axis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1723280,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that disagrees a half of the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1725760,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's one third, which\nis roughly equal to 33%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1729840,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is a different number\nfrom the quantum one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1732880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When our scheming local\nparticles are interrogated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1736000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their answers for\ndifferent questions match"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1738640,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just a little too often."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740480,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They simply can't fake the results"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1742480,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Copenhagen quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744960,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So Bell's proof showed that non-local"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1748000,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and local theories make\ndifferent predictions about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1750320,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how often the two results will disagree,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1752320,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the experimenters\nmeasure different axes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755520,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Non-local quantum mechanics\npredicts disagreement only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1758240,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "25% of the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1760160,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Local hidden variables\npredicts disagreement at least"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1763120,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "33% of the time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1765040,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to find out if there really\nis a local hidden variable theory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1768560,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you just need\nto do the experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1771280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay, so welcome at\nthe Institut d'Optique."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1776000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are here in the place\nwhere Alain Aspect performed forty years ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1780560,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his experiments on the measurement\nof Bell's inequalities,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1783200,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and here are some of the original pictures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1785200,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1786280,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which was much more\nchallenging than it is today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1790400,
    "dDurationMs": 6878,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it was a real\nexperimental tour de force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1797278,
    "dDurationMs": 3122,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So is this one of the\noriginal equipment from that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1800400,
    "dDurationMs": 8240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is one of the,\nyeah, of the polarizers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1808640,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It looks like that now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1811280,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So only on this small breadboard, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1816720,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is our main source"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1818640,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this beam is directed\ntowards this element,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1822080,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the key element of the setup."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1823760,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's a pair of crystals\nthat produces pairs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1826400,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of entangled photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1828960,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We will produce a pair\nof entangled photons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1832960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and both are propagating\nalong each of these two arms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1837280,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're separated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1839120,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here we have the two detection arms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1841600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we can rotate the halfway plate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1844880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to change the orientation\nof the measurement basis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1849120,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The experiment that we did\nwith light was a little bit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1852480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "different from the one we\ndescribed earlier with electrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1855120,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and protons, so I'm gonna\nexplain how they correspond."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1858560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's a little diagram\nof the photon experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1861840,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So first, we have this element\nthat makes the entangled pair"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1865200,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of particles, so that's these two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1869120,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the entangled\nparticles go off on separate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1872560,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arms of the experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1874240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In our previous experiment,\nwe could decide the direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1876880,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we're going to\nmeasure the particles in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1879120,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by rotating the Stern–Gerlach machines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1882080,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in this experiment, it's\nactually really similar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1884640,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we have these two\npolarizers that we're able"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1888320,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to rotate independently,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1890480,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that is gonna decide\nwhich direction these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1893520,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles are measured in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1895600,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so this experiment with\nlight is completely equivalent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1898720,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to Bell's experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1899920,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Bell expected that the, that\nthe experiments would show"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1904160,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the predictions of\nquantum mechanics were correct"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1907200,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that, you know, there was some kind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1908640,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of non-locality in nature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1910040,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Before the first Bell test was done."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1912000,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "John Bell said, in view\nof the general success"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1914160,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quantum mechanics,\nit's very hard for me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1916320,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to doubt the outcome of such experiments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1917840,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- He didn't expect quantum\nphysics to be wrong,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1919920,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because who would bet against quantum physics?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1922240,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'd have to be crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1923160,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Remember, the two different outcomes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1924960,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for Bell's theorem depend on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1926960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how often two different\nmeasurement axes are going"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1931280,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to have results that\ndisagree with each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1935520,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's how we measure\nthat disagreement rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1938400,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, we're gonna start with both"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1940160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the measurements being\nin the same direction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1943440,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and now we expect that these\ntwo are always gonna disagree"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1946080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with each other because\nthey have opposite spins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1948560,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Though we're gonna create a\nbunch of entangled particles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1951200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and find out how many of them disagree"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1953600,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with each other per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1955840,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is going to give us a\nmeasure of the total number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1958880,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of particles coming per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1961520,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because this device is making loads"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1964160,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and loads of entangled particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1966400,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so we just need to know how many"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1967840,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of them are coming at a time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1969360,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then we rotate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1975760,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of the axes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1978080,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and now we measure the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1979840,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of disagreeing pairs per second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1983120,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then dividing these two will give us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1985680,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the disagreement rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1987280,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And remember, quantum mechanics predicts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1989280,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the disagreement rate\nwill only be a quarter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1992320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas local hidden\nvariables expects this number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1995760,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be a third."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1997400,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So I started at 2000, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2003520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now I have five, 500.\nSo that's basically perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2007600,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's, that really\nworks. Pretty well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2009760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We did do this experiment again,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2011760,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the number, we got very much agreed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2014480,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2021360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this is one of the most\nmisunderstood experiments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2024400,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in all of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2025600,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You'll find in all sorts of\nphysics textbooks and papers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2028720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and whatnot, that what\nBell's theorem proves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2032560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it rules out local hidden\nvariables or local realism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2037520,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "John Bell said that\nwas an error, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2042240,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he, he said like, it's\nreally quite remarkable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2044640,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how many people make that error."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2046240,
    "dDurationMs": 4311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I always get confused at the\nconclusion of Bell's theorem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2050551,
    "dDurationMs": 569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah.\n- Because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2051120,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a lot of people who say like, okay,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2052560,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it rules out hidden variables,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2054320,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or things have to be\nnone local or whatever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2058080,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what, what do you think?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2059840,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, I think it is super confusing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2062000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when I first learned\nBell's theorem, I was told"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2064880,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it rules out local hidden variables."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2066520,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I've heard this other\nargument that it's sort"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2068480,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of disproves either locality or realism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2071680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you say, okay, it means\nthat you give up local realism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2077040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so that means you\nsomehow have a choice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2078960,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between giving up locality\nand giving up realism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2081360,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're giving up\nrealism. Realism about what?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2085200,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, like you gotta, you gotta tell me,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2088000,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because like for most\ndefinitions of that word,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2092320,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'd also be giving up locality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2094000,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what the hell are you saving?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2097280,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, I just don't, yeah, it's,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2100720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's a really deep misunderstanding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2102880,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that shows up in almost every single"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2104480,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "textbook on the subject."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2105680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So what does Bell's\ntheorem really prove?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2108880,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, here's the logic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2110480,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Start by assuming locality\nfor the entangled particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2113600,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using the EPR argument,\nthe only way for them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2116080,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to coordinate their outcomes is using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2117840,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "local hidden variables."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2119360,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then Bell's proof showed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2120720,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that local hidden variables\npredict an incorrect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2122960,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experimental result."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2124400,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, the assumption of\nlocality must have been wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2127640,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We are obliged to invoke\nsomething like actions going"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2131040,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faster than light from\none place to another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2133320,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The EPR paper by itself had shown"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2135600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the Copenhagen\nInterpretation is non-local,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2138000,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is why Einstein thought\nthere must be an alternative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2140320,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way to describe the\nexperiment that is local."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2142800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Bell's theorem says that's not true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2145600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any theory that correctly\ndescribes this experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2148000,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must be non-local."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2148960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But I, I still, I would\nhesitate to say that that means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2152400,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Einstein was wrong, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2154800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because what I would, I\nwould say is this shows"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2156800,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Einstein was right to be\nconcerned about all of this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2160640,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- People often claim that\nEinstein's problem was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2163360,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that he simply couldn't\naccept quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2166000,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it was only because he refused"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2168080,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to shut up and calculate that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2169840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He discovered two of the\nmost important aspects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2172240,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quantum mechanics,\nentanglement, and non-locality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2176080,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The heart of the debate between Einstein"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2179680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Bohr was about whether\nthere was a problem,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2184320,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether there was something\nto be concerned about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2188240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the major concern\nthat Einstein brought"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2192480,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the table from the\nbeginning was about locality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2196320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you know what Bell showed\nwas, oh yeah, all that stuff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2200480,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Einstein was concerned\nabout, about locality,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2203200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was completely right\nto be worried about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2206240,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2207760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If these particles really\nare acting non-locally,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2211280,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this should cause paradoxes, shouldn't it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2213920,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it does, but the paradox seems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2216240,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be surprisingly tame."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2218240,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine you and your\nfriend are measuring a pair"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2220160,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of entangled particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2221760,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suppose an observer sees\nyou measure yours first,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2224320,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then your friend measures hers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2226560,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That observer thinks that you\ncollapse the overall state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2228880,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of both particles and your\nfriend just finds out the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2231120,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "result when she measures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2232560,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But another observer will\nsee the situation in reverse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2235680,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They see her measure first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2237120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then you, to them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2238720,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was her measurement\nthat caused the collapse, not yours."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2241840,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But who's right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2242880,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which measurement was\nthe cause of the collapse"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2244800,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and which was the effect?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2246480,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems to depend on\nyour frame of reference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2249920,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This paradox is worrying,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2251680,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it isn't as bad"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2252960,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the usual faster than\nlight paradoxes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2255520,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In relativity,\nyou can communicate faster than light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2258240,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you can exploit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2259360,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how different observers\ndisagree about timing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2262080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your friend who's on a\nrocket sends you an instant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2264560,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "message and you send an instant\nmessage back in some frames"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2267520,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of reference, your message can arrive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2269200,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before she even sent the first one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2271280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your message says, don't\nsend your original message,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2274160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so she doesn't, then\nyou've got yourself a paradox."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2277280,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What prompted you to send this\nmessage if she never sent you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2280000,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anything in the first place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2281600,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum mechanics\nsidesteps these paradoxes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2283920,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through a fundamental constraint."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2286000,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The outcomes are random,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2287920,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you can't send messages\nfaster than light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2290720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you measure your\nparticle, you get a plus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2292880,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a minus completely at random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2294960,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your friend measuring their particle also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2297040,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets a random result."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2298560,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the results will be correlated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2300880,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there's still completely random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2302800,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there's no way to send\nany faster than light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2305920,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "message in this way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2307200,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's what prevents us from\nsending messages back in time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2309760,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "using quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2311120,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So quantum mechanics is non-local,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2313600,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it doesn't lead to the sort"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2315760,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of catastrophic paradoxes you\nmight expect from relativity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2319600,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's an uneasy truce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2321680,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum mechanics may not break the letter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2323600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of relativity laws, but it\ncertainly violates the spirit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2326880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And non-locality isn't\nthe only troubling thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2329280,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2330320,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Copenhagen interpretation\nstill doesn't explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2332560,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what an electron is really doing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2334640,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and why it acts so\ndifferently when measured,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2337920,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "despite this many physicists\ntook Bell's theorem to mean"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2340720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the Copenhagen\ninterpretation was right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2342880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All along Bell himself rejected this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2346560,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He spent the rest of his\nlife championing alternative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2349280,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interpretations of quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2350960,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including the hidden variable\ninterpretation called pilot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2353600,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wave theory or Bohmian mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2355840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bell's theorem doesn't rule\nthis interpretation out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2358320,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the pilot wave\ntheory is non-local,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2360400,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like the Copenhagen interpretation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2363360,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was Bell's theorem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2364400,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and bell's, subsequent tireless work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2366320,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that made studying the meaning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2367600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quantum mechanics\nrespectable again, he showed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2370000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that mere armchair philosophy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2372000,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and thought experiments can have real"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2374320,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consequences in physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2375640,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We need to be teaching quantum\nphysics in a different way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2378160,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We need to be teaching Bell's\ntheorem in a different way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2380240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We do often teach Bell's\ntheorem to physics students,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2384480,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's taught as\nsomething that rules out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2386240,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "local hidden variables."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2387680,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's just not true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2390560,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bell's theorem, you know, says"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2393520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that quantum physics is\nin very serious tension"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2398080,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with relativity on the issue of locality,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2401000,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- John Bell passed away\nsuddenly at the age of 62."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2405360,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He didn't know it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2406640,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but he had been nominated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2407760,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the Nobel Prize just a year earlier"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2409800,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- In a talk he gave in\nGeneva in January, 1990."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2414240,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He said, I think you're\nstuck with the non-locality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2419200,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't know any conception\nof locality, which works"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2422560,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2425040,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That was eight months before he died."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2428480,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So pretty much his last\nword on the subject."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2430600,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And so that's it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2432320,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There really are faster than light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2434080,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "influences in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2435840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bell's theorem proves it,\nbut maybe there is a way out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2441280,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is another way to\ninterpret quantum mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2443520,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's even more bizarre than\nthe Copenhagen interpretation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2446560,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine the EPR thought\nexperiment again, we can think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2449920,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the entangled state as\nbeing in a superposition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2452160,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the electron being up\nand the positron down,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2454720,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the electron being down,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2455920,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the positron being up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2457680,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the Copenhagen interpretation,\nwhen you measure a particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2460480,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you get only one result,\nsay plus, the other part"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2463520,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the superposition collapses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2465600,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in our examples, we've seen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2467120,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that measurement collapse seems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2468560,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be the source of non-locality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2470560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why don't we just get\nrid of collapse altogether?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2473440,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what the many\nworld's interpretation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2475120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of quantum mechanics proposes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2476720,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you measure a particle, instead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2478160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of you collapsing the\nparticle to one outcome,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2480800,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both outcomes happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2482160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there's two parallel versions of you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2484800,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who sees each outcome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2486640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have become entangled\nwith your particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2489120,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because your state depends on\nwhat the particle is doing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2491920,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It sounds strange,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2492960,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there's one huge benefit\nof this interpretation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2495760,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When your friend is about\nto measure her electron,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2498240,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your positron doesn't need to rush"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2500000,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to tell the electron\nwhat the answer will be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2502080,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are already two\nversions of the electron,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2504320,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they contain the right\nanswer for each version of her."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2507840,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was no need for fast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2509120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the like communication to\nexplain the EPR experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2512640,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how is that possible?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2514480,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Doesn't bell's theorem prove"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2515840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the two particles must\ncommunicate faster than light?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2519040,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in Bell's proof, we assumed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2520880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that all measurements\nhave just one outcome,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2523040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that assumption just\nisn't true in many worlds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2526320,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that technically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2527600,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that proof doesn't even apply\nin the many worlds case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2531120,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So is many worlds local?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2533440,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In one sense, no,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2534720,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because just like in\nCopenhagen, quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2536960,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entangled pairs can be\nseparated by a huge distance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2540000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and still share their state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2542000,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, it is local, unlike\nCopenhagen in the sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2545040,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that these far away entangled\nparticles do not influence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2548160,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each other faster than light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2550080,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many worlds obeys Einstein's\nuniversal speed limit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2553600,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is it really worth accepting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2554960,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there are many versions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2555920,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of you in parallel universes\njust to recover locality?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2559360,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, locality isn't the only\nreason many worlds has become"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2562240,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more and more popular."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2563520,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I also really like many worlds, I,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2565280,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because Copenhagen never sits, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2567760,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when you start telling\nthe story, right, of like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2570640,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what happens at measurement,\nit's like, well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2572800,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what is a measurement when you\nhave like this quantum system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2575520,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there's some other system\nwhich is like much larger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2578400,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2579920,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it, it always feels\na little bit arbitrary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2582320,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whereas this, this argument"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2583440,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that every time two quantum\nparticles are interacting,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2586800,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their wave functions are\nessentially, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2589040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combining and becoming entangled,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2592320,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that to me feels more consistent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2593960,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes.\nBut I, I think that's right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2596000,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do you think are like\nthe problems with many worlds?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2598440,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The biggest problem is I\nthink people's struggle to deal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2603040,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with sort of the infinity that that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2605200,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brings forth.\n- For sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2606400,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But I, I don't know that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2607600,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's necessarily an argument against it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2609360,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just 'cause like, just 'cause it's hard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2610640,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to imagine doesn't mean, yeah,\nit's not what's happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2613920,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If many worlds is right,\neverything changes the conflict"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2617600,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between quantum mechanics\nand relativity vanishes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2620720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Physicists have been\nstruggling for decades"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2623360,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to unite quantum mechanics\nwith general relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2626000,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to build a theory of quantum gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2628480,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And maybe we've been failing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2629840,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we've been trying\nto marry relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2632080,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a non-local theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2634000,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if quantum mechanics\nultimately turns out to be local,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2636960,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then Einstein's dream\nof a local description"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2639840,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of reality might not be dead,\nafter all."
    } ]
  } ]
}
